1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,184
Ever solve a problem in the shower that

2
00:00:02,184 --> 00:00:03,219
beat you all week?

3
00:00:03,269 --> 00:00:04,681
Congratulations.

4
00:00:04,731 --> 00:00:07,058
You're Specimen 003.

5
00:00:07,367 --> 00:00:09,660
Scientists finally figured out why.

6
00:00:09,710 --> 00:00:10,622
And no...

7
00:00:11,122 --> 00:00:12,495
it's not the shampoo.

8
00:00:12,800 --> 00:00:13,808
Observe.

9
00:00:13,858 --> 00:00:15,508
At the desk: nothing.

10
00:00:15,558 --> 00:00:17,518
Under warm water: everything.

11
00:00:17,833 --> 00:00:19,404
It tried thinking harder.

12
00:00:19,454 --> 00:00:20,833
It tried more coffee.

13
00:00:20,883 --> 00:00:21,749
Nothing.

14
00:00:22,067 --> 00:00:23,686
Then the water turns on...

15
00:00:24,186 --> 00:00:26,529
and the mind is finally free to wander.

16
00:00:27,700 --> 00:00:29,892
Scientists call it the shower effect.

17
00:00:30,200 --> 00:00:34,654
In 2022, researchers gave over 300 people a

18
00:00:34,654 --> 00:00:35,950
creativity test.

19
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:37,848
Then they made them watch a video.

20
00:00:38,167 --> 00:00:40,238
Some watched two men hanging laundry.

21
00:00:40,288 --> 00:00:42,328
Others watched a scene from a movie.

22
00:00:42,633 --> 00:00:45,347
Only the movie group's wandering minds got more

23
00:00:45,347 --> 00:00:46,204
creative.

24
00:00:46,533 --> 00:00:48,306
So the secret isn't boredom.

25
00:00:48,356 --> 00:00:50,696
It's a task that's just interesting enough.

26
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:51,862
A walk.

27
00:00:51,912 --> 00:00:53,226
Washing dishes.

28
00:00:53,276 --> 00:00:54,183
A shower.

29
00:00:54,233 --> 00:00:55,337
Not your phone.

30
00:00:55,387 --> 00:00:56,950
That one's too interesting.

31
00:00:58,133 --> 00:01:00,590
Maybe the answer doesn't need more effort.

32
00:01:00,840 --> 00:01:02,288
Just a little space.

33
00:01:02,600 --> 00:01:05,071
Sadly, the specimen still has no pen.

34
00:01:05,071 --> 00:01:06,354
Perfectly human.
